{"reference":"Job 18","book":"Job","chapter":18,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Debate Around Bildad’s Speech","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Bildad’s description of the wicked person’s ruin belongs to the sustained debate that follows Job’s initial lament. Job’s friends increasingly treat suffering as evidence of wrongdoing, while Job rejects that diagnosis. This larger setting matters for reading Bildad’s speech: its fierce images are part of his argument against Job, not an undifferentiated explanation of every sufferer’s condition. The book later rebukes the friends’ counsel, even though they had first shown costly presence by sitting silently with Job.","verse_refs":["Job 10:1-22","Job 11:1-20","Job 12:1-25","Job 13:1-28","Job 14:1-22","Job 15:1-35","Job 16:1-22","Job 17:1-16","Job 19:1-29","Job 1:1-22","Job 20:1-29","Job 21:1-34","Job 22:1-30","Job 23:1-17","Job 24:1-25","Job 25:1-6","Job 26:1-14","Job 27:1-23","Job 28:1-28","Job 29:1-25","Job 2:1-13","Job 2:11-13","Job 30:1-31","Job 31:1-40","Job 32:1-22","Job 33:1-33","Job 34:1-37","Job 35:1-16","Job 36:1-33","Job 37:1-24","Job 38:1-41","Job 39:1-30","Job 3:1-26","Job 40:1-24","Job 41:1-34","Job 42:1-17","Job 4:1-21","Job 5:1-27","Job 6:1-30","Job 7:1-21","Job 8:1-22","Job 9:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_job_018_caa6414b6208b3a6ccb778cb"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_2","text":"Later reflection on Job connects his suffering with endurance and with the Lord’s compassionate outcome. In this broader sense, Job’s steadfastness refers to persistence through the story; it should not be read as a demand for silent endurance of abuse or as a prohibition against seeking safety and protection.","verse_refs":["Job 10:1-22","Job 11:1-20","Job 12:1-25","Job 13:1-28","Job 14:1-22","Job 15:1-35","Job 16:1-22","Job 17:1-16","Job 19:1-29","Job 1:1-22","Job 20:1-29","Job 21:1-34","Job 22:1-30","Job 23:1-17","Job 24:1-25","Job 25:1-6","Job 26:1-14","Job 27:1-23","Job 28:1-28","Job 29:1-25","Job 2:1-13","Job 2:11-13","Job 30:1-31","Job 31:1-40","Job 32:1-22","Job 33:1-33","Job 34:1-37","Job 35:1-16","Job 36:1-33","Job 37:1-24","Job 38:1-41","Job 39:1-30","Job 3:1-26","Job 40:1-24","Job 41:1-34","Job 42:1-17","Job 4:1-21","Job 5:1-27","Job 6:1-30","Job 7:1-21","Job 8:1-22","Job 9:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_job_018_74212ba2472a5408eef6e9ed"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}